# synthetic inter-file newline required)
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmmfc.seq/casmmfd.seq fixture
# pair in cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM.
# Assemble with: CASM CASMMFC.S CASMMFD.S /O:CASMMF2.PRG
#
# File C (.ORG $C000) has NO trailing newline after "LDA VALD" -- sourceLoad
# must insert one synthetic LF between the files, or "LDA VALD" and
# "VALD: RTS" would silently concatenate onto one (invalid) line. The
# logical program is otherwise identical to casmmf1's:
#   LDA VALD           ; forward reference -- forces absolute (3 bytes)
# File D:
#   label VALD, opcode RTS -- VALD resolves to $C000 + 3 = $C003
#
# Hand assembly (byte-identical to casmmf1's, proving the synthetic
# separator produces the same result as an author-supplied newline would):
#   00 C0        PRG load-address header ($C000, little-endian)
#   AD 03 C0     LDA $C003   (forced absolute; resolves to VALD)
#   60           RTS         (at $C003, defines VALD)
